        <p class="profile-detail-region">City · South &amp; Southeast Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Pataliputra</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 490 BCE – c. 637 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Built by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magadha">Magadha</a> ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajatashatru">Ajatashatru</a> in 490 BCE as a small fort, Pataligrama, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>; other sources credit <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udayin">Udayin</a> or Udayabhadra with founding the city, and archaeology shows urban development no earlier than the 3rd or 4th century BCE.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">At the confluence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>, Gandhaka and Son rivers, beside modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patna">Patna</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">A water fort at a river confluence; capital of the Nandas, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Mauryas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Guptas</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/megasthenes">Megasthenes</a>' account of its wooden walls and 64 gates; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka</a>'s Buddhist council; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faxian">Faxian</a>'s hospitals; its decline and abandonment</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Much of the ancient city lies buried beneath modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patna">Patna</a>, and parts of it have been excavated at Kumhrar, Bulandi Bagh and Agam Kuan.</span></div>
        </div>
